#. macro: <if ($n2 > 0)> (<num $n1>/<num $n2>)</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = number parameter 2 > 0 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <num $n1> — a number; value = number parameter 1 (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <num $n2> — a number; value = number parameter 2 (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <if ($n1 == $n2)></ui-edge-color></ui-color></if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = number parameter 1 == number parameter 2 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: </ui-edge-color> — end of: text outline color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-edge-color> restores the previous color (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
